  "body": "### What is the issue with the Streams Standard?\n\n[close](https://streams.spec.whatwg.org/#readablestream-close) performs ! ReadableByteStreamControllerClose(controller).\n\nFetch can hit this assert when a network body ends, for example with a 1-byte response:\n\n```js\nconst response = await fetch(\"/one-byte\");\nawait response.body.getReader({ mode: \"byob\" }).read(new Uint16Array(1));\n```\n\nThrown from https://streams.spec.whatwg.org/#readable-byte-stream-controller-close (4.2.3).\n\nFileAPI usage can also hit it (though technically it does not invoke close currently https://github.com/w3c/FileAPI/issues/206).\n\nThe byte goes into the pending pull into, then Fetch closes the stream, and the close throws.\n\nI believe we can just return early if it throws an abrupt completion here.",
